Why Is Demand Increasing
Industrial Water Reuse — Growing pressure to conserve freshwater resources is increasing the use of electrodialysis for industrial wastewater treatment, demineralization, process-water conditioning, and water reuse.
Resource Recovery — Electrodialysis is expanding beyond conventional water treatment into lithium recovery, selective ion separation, acid and base recovery, and other resource-recovery applications.
High-Purity Processing — Pharmaceutical, food, semiconductor, and other high-purity industries require precise ionic separation, creating demand for advanced membrane-based systems.

Water Technology & Resource Recovery Watch
Electrodialysis is evolving from a conventional demineralization technology into a broader electrically driven separation platform. Continuous systems remain important for large industrial throughput, while bipolar and selective membrane technologies are opening applications in chemical recovery, lithium processing, and high-value separations. System integration, membrane selection, pilot testing, and lifecycle economics are increasingly important factors when evaluating projects.

